      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T17:46:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "l.98 describes support for curve 25519, which behaves differently than the NIST curves (P-224, P-256 etc).   In particular, the encoding of curve points is different for Ed25519 signing (twisted Edwards curve) than for X25519 key agreement (Montgomery curve), so the same key can\u0027t be used for both (unlike the NIST curves).\n\n(But not disagreeing that it\u0027s a bit hard to follow...)",
